# Preflight Status

The preflight status file is the ephemeral result of one Preflight run. It lives at `memory-bank/active/.preflight-status`. Overwrite it each run. Delete it at archive.

**First line** is exactly one of these (exact casing):

- `PASS` — checks passed with no advisories
- `PASS WITH ADVISORY` — checks passed; advisory findings recorded; still a valid build/transition gate; includes in-phase plan edits
- `FAIL (fixable)` — plan has issues but the issues have known fixes; planner re-plans.
- `FAIL (blocking)` — plan has issues that require materially changing the plan; operator must provide guidance then invoke `/niko-plan`.

After a blank line, the rest of the file is this run's findings, in prose. No required headings.
